<title>USA: Procter &amp; Gamble settles patent lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Procter &amp; Gamble settles patent lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co said on Friday it had settled a lawsuit it filed against Bradley Pharmaceuticals Inc alleging infringement of a P&amp;G ulcer drug patent.</p>
<p>As part of the settlement, Bradley has agreed to stop marketing its ulcer drug. P&amp;G said. Other terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>P&amp;G filed the suit in June over a Bradley product kit containing bismuth subsalicylate, metronidazole and tetracycline, which was billed as a treatment of ulcer diseases caused by Helicobacter pylori bacterial infections.  </p>
<p>P&amp;G said its patent covers therapies using that drug combination.</p>
</text>
